Replace the hosts a secret may be injected to
(PUT /v1/vault/secrets/{name}/allowed-hosts).

The list is replaced, not added to. Narrowing it takes effect in seconds: the
host agents poll for narrowed authorization and drop the cached value, rather
than waiting out its TTL.

A secret stored before allowed hosts existed has none recorded, and nothing may
use it until this command sets a list.

Usage:
  anona-compute vault allowed-hosts <name> [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help               help for allowed-hosts
      --host stringArray   a host this secret may be sent to (repeatable; required)

Global Flags:
      --api-key string             API key (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_KEY, E2B_API_KEY)
      --api-url string             API URL (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_URL, E2B_API_URL; default https://api.<E2B_DOMAIN>)
      --json                       JSON output: one object per line on stdout (same as -o json)
  -o, --output string              output format: text or json (default "text")
      --profile string             config profile to use (env ANONA_COMPUTE_PROFILE; default "default")
      --request-timeout duration   timeout for each API request (0 = none)
  -v, --verbose                    verbose output on stderr
